d_at":null},"comments":2,"created_at":"2023-01-29T00:59:23Z","updated_at":"2023-01-30T17:20:59Z","closed_at":"2023-01-30T17:20:58Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Describe the typing issue\n\nThe type hint for `with_for_update(of=elem)` appears to be incorrect. It should accept ORM tables instances\n\n### To Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom sqlalchemy import Integer, Select, select\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import DeclarativeBase, Mapped, mapped_column\r\n\r\n\r\nclass Base(DeclarativeBase):\r\n    pass\r\n\r\n\r\nclass Table(Base):\r\n    __tablename__ = \"table\"\r\n\r\n    id: Mapped[int] = mapped_column(Integer, primary_key=True)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef query() -> Select[tuple[Table]]:\r\n    return select(\r\n        Table,\r\n    ).with_for_update(\r\n        of=Table,\r\n    )\n```\n\n\n### Error\n\n```\r\nerror: Argument \"of\" to \"with_for_update\" of \"GenerativeSelect\" has incompatible type \"Type[Table]\"; expected \"Union[_HasClauseElement, SQLCoreOperations[Any], ExpressionElementRole[Any], Callable[[], ColumnElement[Any]], LambdaElement, Sequence[Union[ColumnElement[Any], _HasClauseElement, SQLCoreOperations[Any], ExpressionElementRole[Any], Callable[[], ColumnElement[Any]], LambdaElement]], None]\"  [arg-type]\r\n``` \n\n### Versions\n\n- OS: Ubuntu 22.04\r\n- Python: 3.11\r\n- SQLAlchemy: 2.0.0\r\n- Type checker: mypy 0.991\r\n\n\n### Additional context\n\n_No response_","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/s